// Program 1: Test if 0 is treated as false.

if (0) {
    print "true";
} else {
    print "false";
}

// Expected:
// I expected this to print "false" because languages like C treat 0 as false.

// Actual:
// It prints "true".

// Why:
// In Lox, only false and nil are falsey.
// Every other value, including 0, is considered true.